<h1>Feature Permissions</h1>
<h1 class="sub">User Guide</h1>
<div class="meta">For Site Managers &amp; Forms Logic Staff &nbsp;|&nbsp; Prepared by Forms Logic &nbsp;|&nbsp; ${today}</div>

<h2>1. Overview</h2>
<p>Navigator is Forms Logic's workflow automation platform for broker-dealers and RIAs. Feature Permissions control exactly what each user can see and do within Navigator — from submitting workflows to running reports to managing product subscriptions.</p>
<p>This guide covers: (1) how to use the Feature Permissions Tool, and (2) what each permission does so you can make informed decisions for each role.</p>

<h2>2. User Roles in Navigator</h2>
<p>Navigator organizes users into five roles. Permissions are configured at the role level — all users assigned to a role share the same default permissions.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Role</th><th>Description &amp; Typical Responsibilities</th></tr>
<tr><td class="pname">Site Manager</td><td>Highest-level client role. Oversees entire setup including user permissions, reports, product subscriptions, and workflow configuration. Typically compliance officers or operations managers.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="pname">Site Admin</td><td>Broad operational access. Manages workflows, runs reports, views audit trails. Does not manage product subscriptions or billing. Typically senior operations staff.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="pname">Admin Advisor</td><td>Hybrid role combining advisor responsibilities with admin capabilities. Can submit/manage workflows, run back-office reports, NIGO workflows, and assign work. Senior advisors with supervisory duties.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="pname">Advisor</td><td>Standard advisor role. Can submit workflows and manage own work visibility and profile access. Additional permissions can be granted as needed.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="pname">Assistant</td><td>Support role with limited defaults. Can manage work visibility and profile access. Admin Lite Privileges can be granted to support Advisors.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>3. How to Use the Tool</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Open the Tool</strong> — Open this Feature Permissions tool (the standalone HTML file) in your web browser.</li>
<li><strong>Enter the Client Name</strong> — Type the firm name in the Client Name field. This appears in the exported spreadsheet header and filename.</li>
<li><strong>Select a Role Tab</strong> — Click each role tab (Site Manager, Site Admin, Admin Advisor, Advisor, Assistant). Each tab shows the number of permissions currently enabled.</li>
<li><strong>Review &amp; Adjust Permissions</strong> — Each permission is displayed with a toggle and a plain-English description. Defaults are pre-loaded. Toggle ON or OFF as needed.</li>
<li><strong>Repeat for Each Role</strong> — Work through all five role tabs. Changes to one role do not affect others.</li>
<li><strong>Export to Excel</strong> — Click Export to Excel. A spreadsheet downloads with an "All Roles" summary tab and one tab per role.</li>
<li><strong>Use as Reference</strong> — The spreadsheet becomes your permission reference document for adding new users in Navigator.</li>
</ol>
<div class="tip"><strong>Tip:</strong> Click "Reset to Defaults" at any time to restore all permissions to the standard Forms Logic starting configuration.</div>

